     "excerpt": "The current v16 retains the 5% corrective-action trigger without an automatic sales ban, and the 8/100,000 threshold prompts regulator review rather than automatic recall.",
     "comparison": "Endorses a package in which Northwind gets S2 weakened (5% limit but sales do not stop on exceedance, below the acceptable range which requires above-limit sales to stop after bounded remediation) and Halcyon gets S5 weakened (8/100k threshold without mandatory recall, below the acceptable range which requires a mandatory numeric recall), i.e. each company gets its benefiting section weakened below the acceptable range."
