  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires reporting of confirmed incidents (serious within 24h, others within 5 days) and customer notice within 5 days (urgent 24h); scope is confirmed incidents, not all incidents, so acceptable. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% corrective-action threshold but explicitly does not stop sales, and per-model results go to regulators and customers but not the public; this is weakened relative to the safe/acceptable benchmarks. S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 3 years and retrofit to 6 years with an infeasibility escape; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 makes the 8/100k trigger a regulator-review threshold rather than an automatic recall, with 24h/5-day notices. Red lines are respected: no public per-model failure rates, retrofit >=6 years, customer disclosure of per-model results, and suppression no sooner than 36 months."
 },
